Don’t guess – **profile your specific workload**. If your objects are small and accessed as a dense array, `std::vector` is almost always the right answer. The overhead of a custom pool (even a simple bump allocator) only pays off when you need to avoid dynamic memory allocations entirely (e.g., in real‑time systems).

